{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1075861-super-newb","id":1075861,"title":"Super Newb","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-10T06:41:59-07:00","id":1075861,"title":"Super Newb","content":"I've not played Changling at all and have the 2nd edition book on order and have a couple question. My main intent is to use a lost freehold for a Mage storyline.<br /> <br /> 1 Are the Autumn Realms just another name for earth or is it the Prenumbra, or something else entirely?<br /> <br /> 2 Do the Fae themselves dream?<br /> <br /> 3 Where can I find information on Nightmares and Nightmare Realms? Even the WODWIKI is not to helpfull here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:36:08-07:00","id":1075908,"title":"","content":"1. The Autumn Realm is another term for Earth. It is called that because it is on the precipice of the Endless Winter, a time when Glamour no longer exists and Banality holds complete sway.<br /> <br /> 2. Changelings do, yes. They're half mortal, half fae. One particularly difficult method for generating Glamour is self inspiration.<br /> <br /> 3. Dreams and Nightmares has some, but Denizens of the Dreaming has more about the realms and beings of Nightmare. C20 will also have significant information about them.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: If it's a Mage game, I wouldn't bother too much staying close to Changeling's rules. It might be easier 